---
paths:
  references: references/
  reference_notes: reference-notes/
  literature_notes: literature-notes/
  permanent_notes: permanent-notes/
  maps: maps/
  sources: sources/
  index: .slipbox-index/

# Index/embeddings/search are handled by QMD (github.com/tobi/qmd).
# Set the embedding model in .qmd/index.yml or via QMD_EMBED_MODEL.
qmd:
  collection: slipbox
  search_mode: query

clustering:
  method: hdbscan
  min_cluster_size: 4

notes:
  id_style: timestamp
  link_style: wikilink
  frontmatter: yaml
---

# House style

- Write literature notes as a single atomic idea in plain, first-person prose.
- Keep notes short — if it needs two ideas, make two notes.
- Tag with lowercase, hyphenated topics.
- Always link a note back to its source reference.
- Favor connections: when a new note relates to an existing one, link them.
